1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,310
Some people say that dogs are man’s best friend – good companions, loyal and loveable.
有人说，狗是人类最好的朋友——它们是贴心的伙伴，忠诚又惹人喜爱。

2
00:00:08,310 --> 00:00:14,910
Of course, they can be more than just a pet as certain breeds are excellent working dogs too.
当然，狗的作用远不止是宠物，有些品种还是出色的工作犬。

3
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:27,650
We know about the amazing help guide dogs give to blind people and, more recently, a new role has been found for the animals – working as therapy dogs in universities.
我们都知道导盲犬能为盲人提供极大的帮助，而近来，人们又为狗狗们找到了一个新角色——在大学里担任治疗犬。

4
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:36,910
Research by Washington State University in the US, has found spending time with a pooch can help stressed out students.
美国华盛顿州立大学的一项研究发现，和狗狗相处能帮助压力山大的学生缓解焦虑。

5
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:58,060
Patricia Pendry from the university told the BBC that a study of 300 undergraduates had found weekly hour-long sessions with dogs brought to the university by professional handlers had made stressed students at "high risk of academic failure" or dropping out, "feel relaxed and accepted".
该校的帕特里夏·彭德里向英国广播公司表示，一项针对300名本科生的研究显示，由专业驯养员带进校园的狗狗，每周和学生进行一次时长一小时的互动，可以让那些“面临高危辍学压力风险”的学生“感到放松和被接纳”。

6
00:00:58,060 --> 00:01:02,760
The dogs helped them to concentrate, learn and remember information.
狗狗还能帮助他们集中注意力，更好地学习和记忆知识。

7
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:18,600
I know that stroking a dog helps me to relax; other research has shown that petting animals can reduce stress hormone levels and anxiety, so it makes sense to introduce them into an environment where people are stressed.
我知道撸狗能帮我放松；其他研究也表明，抚摸动物可以降低压力激素水平，缓解焦虑情绪。因此，把它们引入压力环境是合理的做法。

8
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:30,170
The BBC’s education correspondent Sean Coughlan writes that around 1,000 campuses in the US already use therapy pets and it’s becoming more common in the UK.
英国广播公司教育记者肖恩·考夫兰写道，美国已有约1000所大学校园配备了治疗宠物，这种做法在英国也正变得越来越普遍。

9
00:01:30,170 --> 00:01:39,260
For example, The University of Middlesex has employed ‘canine teaching assistants’ to help stop lonely students dropping out.
例如，密德萨斯大学就聘请了“犬类教学助理”，帮助孤独的学生避免辍学。

10
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:50,220
Fiona Suthers, head of clinical skills at the university, says that five Labradors had a “stringent assessment” to ensure they had the right temperament.
该校临床技能负责人菲奥娜·萨瑟斯表示，五只拉布拉多犬都经过了“严格的评估”，以确保它们拥有合适的性情。

11
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:57,630
But she adds “it’s hard to describe the impact of just having a dog lying down in the corner of a class.”
但她补充道：“仅仅让一只狗趴在教室角落能产生多大的影响，这还很难说。”

12
00:01:57,630 --> 00:02:02,570
Using dogs for therapy can also help the dogs themselves.
让狗狗参与治疗工作，对它们自身也有好处。

13
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:11,860
In Wales, Swansea University Students’ Union has used rescued greyhounds to help students unwind between exams.
在威尔士，斯旺西大学学生会就利用获救的灵缇犬，帮助学生在考试间隙放松身心。

14
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:19,640
Sessions allow mistreated and abandoned dogs to interact with humans and begin to trust them again.
这些互动环节能让受过虐待和被遗弃的狗狗与人类交流，重新建立对人类的信任。

15
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:35,260
Student Union education officer Chloe Hutchinson told the BBC that “a lot of students have dogs at home and might be a bit homesick, especially around exam time when it is stressful and you just want your home comforts.”
学生会教育干事克洛伊·哈钦森向英国广播公司表示：“很多学生家里都养狗，他们可能会有点想家，尤其是在考试期间，压力很大，就格外想念家里的温馨时光。”

16
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:48,700
So if you’re a student who’s been working like a dog, but you still feel like you haven’t a dog’s chance in passing your exams, maybe introducing a four-legged friend into your life might be the help you need.
所以，如果你是一名学生，已经拼命用功，却仍觉得考试及格无望，或许让一位四条腿的朋友走进你的生活，就是你需要的助力。
